Small Default Big List Cards Table <pre><code>{{ forms.buttonGroup({
    name: "viewMode",
    value: "list",
    options: [
        { label: "List",  value: "list" },
        { label: "Cards", value: "cards" },
        { label: "Table", value: "table" },
    ],
}) }}
</code></pre> <p>Note</p> <p>Icon buttons. Pass <code>icon: "settings"</code> (a Craft icon name) to <code>forms.button</code>. Craft renders an inline SVG inside <code>.cp-icon</code>. Add <code>spinner: true</code> to reserve space for a loading indicator on async actions.</p>

Enable comments  Allow guest authors  Send notifications TwigCopy <pre>{{ forms.checkboxGroupField({
  label: "Options",
  name: "options",
  values: ["comments","notify"],
  options: [
    {label:"Enable comments",value:"comments"},
    {label:"Allow guests",value:"guests"},
    {label:"Send notifications",value:"notify"},
  ],
}) }}</pre>  Draft  Pending review  Published TwigCopy <pre>{{ forms.radioGroupField({
  label: "Status",
  name: "status",
  value: "draft",
  options: [
    {label:"Draft",value:"draft"},
    {label:"Pending review",value:"pending"},
    {label:"Published",value:"live"},
  ],
}) }}</pre>

Choose a new entry type <p>Select which entry type to add to this section. You can reorder and rename types later in the section’s settings.</p> CancelAdd <pre><code>&lt;div class="modal"&gt;
  &lt;div class="header"&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Choose a new entry type&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="body"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Select which entry type to add…&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="footer"&gt;
    &lt;button class="btn"&gt;Cancel&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button class="btn submit"&gt;Add&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

// Float it over a shade and manage focus/escape:
new Garnish.Modal($container, { resizable: false });
</code></pre>

ContentSEOSettings <pre><code>&lt;div id="tabs" class="tabs"&gt;
  &lt;a class="tab sel" href="#content"&gt;Content&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a class="tab" href="#seo"&gt;SEO&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Note</p> <p>In practice. Most plugins never hand-write tabs — you declare them in a controller’s template <code>tabs</code> variable or a field layout, and Craft renders the markup and toggling behavior.</p>

Heading Summary<p>A short teaser for listings.</p>Craft is a flexible, user-friendly CMS. <pre><code>{{ forms.textField({ label: "Heading", name: "heading", value: value }) }}

{{ forms.textareaField({
    label: "Summary",
    instructions: "A short teaser for listings.",
    name: "summary",
    rows: 4,
    value: value,
}) }}
</code></pre>
